"2(i) `disability' means - (i) blindness;
(ii) low vision;
(iii) leprosy-cured;
(iv) hearing impairment;
(v) locomotor disability;
(vi) mental retardation;
(vii) mental illness;
(q) `mental illness' means any mental disorder other than mental retardation;
(r) `mental retardation' means a condition of arrested or incomplete development of the mind of a person, which is specially characterised by subnormality of intelligence."
